00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:07.389 align:start position:0%
ministers of agriculture and fisheries  are expected to discuss a new proposal  by the Commission to bring together and  simplify to currently separate school  schemes the school fruit scheme and the  school milk scheme cutting through the  red tape and setting the funds to 230  million euros per school year the scheme  addresses a worrying trend European  children consume less and less fruit  vegetables and milk products with the  slogan eat well feel good it aims to  counter poor nutrition habits beginning  with children from school age it also  aims to raise awareness of the benefits  of a healthy diet and to fight against  obesity which affects one in three  European kids between six and nine years  old EU ministers will also continue  discussions on the new rules presented  by the Commission to further promote  European agricultural products the  objective is to open up new markets for  these products both on the internal and  export markets and to increase consumer  awareness of their quality finally  ministers will exchange views on the  future of the dairy sector in Europe  following the end of the quota system in  2015
 

